Stop narrowing BF16 matmul rows to F16 when quantizing

Every arm opens with Tensor<FloatType>(from: tensor), which silently converts
BF16 weights to F16. Z-Image and the Qwen family carry CCV_16BF matmul rows
inside their _f16 checkpoints, the codecs keep centroids and row scales in the
tensor's own dtype, and ccv_nnc_tensor_read has no 16F to 16BF path, so the
quantized result crashes the server on its first generation. Pass an
already-16-bit tensor through untouched and narrow only what needs it.

Found by comparing a Z-Image Turbo quantized by this CLI against one the macOS
app produced from the same source. The recipe matched exactly and the only
discrepancy in the whole file was 238 F16 rows where the app had BF16. That
file segfaulted both gRPCServerCLI and the app, while the app's own generated
normally. The app is where BF16 architectures get quantized in practice, which
is why this has gone unnoticed.
